      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.thevillageok.gov/157/About-The-Village",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Village Library began in 1966 inside Casady Square, moved to a standalone building in 1990, and was renovated in 2019.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Village%2C_Oklahoma",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Geographically, The Village is an enclave almost entirely surrounded by Oklahoma City, touching only Nichols Hills on one side.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
